WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.510
Hi.

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:04.070
I'm hifihedgehog, the developer of PadForge.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.110
You're hearing a generated voice.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.130
PadForge is a free Windows app that makes any input look like any controller.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.590
Many PC games only work properly with the controller they expect.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:21.390
PadForge creates virtual controllers that games treat as real hardware,

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.370
and you choose what drives them.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.330
That can be a different controller, a keyboard and mouse,

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.150
a flight stick, your phone's web browser, or your own voice.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.970
PadForge recognizes phrases you set up, offline, with no account.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.410
Every button, stick and trigger can be remapped or turned into a macro,

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.970
and PadForge switches to a game's own profile when that game comes to the front.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.090
PadForge works with a screen reader and from the keyboard.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:53.650
Here is NVDA reading PadForge, one Tab key at a time.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.160
[NVDA] Slot 1, data item, 4 of 5

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.040
[NVDA] Delete virtual controller, button

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:05.010
[NVDA] Enabled, toggle button, pressed, Awaiting devices

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.830
[NVDA] Xbox, radio button, not checked

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.070
[NVDA] PlayStation, radio button, not checked

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.200
[NVDA] Nintendo, radio button, checked

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.250
[NVDA] Settings saved to PadForge.xml.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.760
Every control the Tab key reaches has a spoken name.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.500
Buttons speak their state,

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.500
status changes are announced as they happen, and Escape closes a dialog.

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:31.770
The interface comes in 109 languages, and the spoken names follow the one you pick.

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:38.330
PadForge is free, with no subscription, no paywall and no nag screens.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.050
It runs on Windows 10 and 11, with a preliminary build for Windows 11 on ARM.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.930
Windows asks for administrator permission each time it starts.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.160
Get it at padforge.org.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.780
That's P-A-D, forge, dot org.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:54.610
Thanks for listening.
